      Two routing modes, one rendering model. The first visit is server routing: a complete HTML
      document, content visible before JavaScript. Every navigation after is client routing: the
      router fetches the RSC payload for the changing segments (often already prefetched) and merges
      it in place; layouts, their state, and their containers persist.
